https://github.com/mohaidr/focus-board

Third-party libraries, fonts, and other components keep their own licenses.
Your data and content are yours; this license does not require sharing them.

2. Use and extend Dashora

The Licensors grant everyone a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license
to use, copy, modify, and redistribute the Software under these terms.
Personal, educational, nonprofit, institutional, and commercial use are allowed.
There is no minimum contribution, contributor registration, or separate
commercial approval.

You may use and extend the Software however you wish for your own private use
or your organization's internal use, including internal commercial use.
Private/internal modifications do not have to be published or contributed.
Internal access may include employees and contractors working on behalf of
the organization; it does not include offering the application to customers
or the general public.

You may publish source forks and submit pull requests without waiting for a
merge. Public hosting of a modified application is subject to Section 3.

Keep this license and existing copyright and attribution notices with copies
you distribute. Distribute the Software and modifications to it under this
license, preserving recipients' permissions and obligations. Do not imply
official endorsement of your version.

3. Give back changes you host publicly

You may publicly host an unmodified version of Dashora, whether free or paid,
without making a contribution.

Before publicly hosting a modified version, submit its new features and
functional changes to the Official Repository and have them merged by the
project maintainers. This applies to both free and paid hosting and includes
customer-facing services, even when access requires an account or payment.

A public fork or an open pull request alone does not meet the merge requirement.
There is no additional approval step after the relevant changes are merged.
Each later new feature or functional change must also be merged before you
make it available through your public service.

The merged contribution must include the working source needed to provide
the same feature or functional change in Dashora, with appropriate tests and
documentation. Merely describing a feature or contributing a placeholder is
not enough. Maintainers may review, request changes, or decline contributions;
submission does not guarantee a merge or permission to host unmerged changes.

You do not need to contribute deployment settings, credentials, private data,
or branding-only and cosmetic changes that do not alter functionality.
You do not need to contribute independent software that does not contain or
modify the Software. Do not submit secrets or content you lack permission to
publish.

Make the corresponding source of your publicly hosted modified version,
including its modifications and instructions needed to build and run it,
publicly available under this license. Provide users a clear link to that
source. Secrets and private data must be excluded; example configuration
may be provided instead.

People using your hosted service do not need to contribute separately.
Charging for hosting, support, or services is allowed subject to these terms.

4. Contributions and ownership

You keep ownership of your contributions. By intentionally submitting a
